sequenceDiagram
    participant U as You<br/>User and Chat UI
    participant A as Chat API<br/>and Lifecycle
    participant I as Interaction<br/>Agent
    participant R as Execution Agent<br/>Registry and Search
    participant Q as Durable<br/>Execution Queue
    participant E as Execution<br/>Agents
    participant T as Tools<br/>Gmail and Triggers
    participant K as Task<br/>Search Email
    participant M as Memory<br/>Conversation and Agent Memory
    participant B as Background Services<br/>Monitor, Scheduler, Maintenance
    autonumber
    Note over I,E: The Interaction Agent talks to you and delegates work.<br/>Each Execution Agent is a saved owner of ongoing work.<br/>An execution is one queued run for that Execution Agent.
    Note over E,K: Tools perform atomic operations.<br/>A Task is a complex operation, such as Search Email,<br/>that can use its own model loop and Gmail tools.
    Note over R,M: Conversation Memory is the shared chat used by the Interaction Agent.<br/>Agent Memory belongs to one specific Execution Agent ID.<br/>SQLite journals are authoritative, chat logs are projections.<br/>Shown limits are configurable for one backend process.
    rect rgb(250, 245, 255)
        Note over U,B: 1. Accept the Request and Select Execution Agents
        U->>A: Submit a chat request
        A->>M: Save request and request ID for recovery<br/>after a backend restart
        A-->>U: HTTP 202 accepted, Chat UI polls conversation history
        A->>I: Process the accepted request asynchronously
        I->>M: Read Conversation Memory and recent<br/>Execution Agent references
        M-->>I: Summary and recent chat within 8,000 estimated tokens,<br/>plus up to 10 recent Execution Agent references
        I->>M: Save the Conversation Memory snapshot<br/>with this request for recovery
        alt Answer or clarify without delegating any work
            I-->>U: Save and show a direct answer or clarifying question
        else Delegate work within the user's authorization
            I-->>U: Save and show an acknowledgement before execution finishes
            loop Each delegated work item needs its own selected Execution Agent
                alt Known Execution Agent ID or saved conversation link
                    I->>R: Resolve that Execution Agent's saved identity
                else Discover a suitable Execution Agent
                    I->>R: Search Execution Agent records by keywords,<br/>meaning and identifying references
                    Note over I,R: Filter by connected account, exclude confirmed ID conflicts.<br/>Retrieve up to 30 keyword and 30 semantic candidates.<br/>Semantic search uses OpenRouter embeddings.
                    Note over I,R: Merge by Execution Agent ID using 1 / (60 + rank).<br/>Rank 1 scores more than rank 2, matches in both add scores.<br/>Exact identifying matches come first. Keep up to 30,<br/>show 10 per page. Keyword search survives embedding failure.
                    R-->>I: Compact Execution Agent candidates<br/>and evidence of the work they own
                end
                alt Identity is ambiguous, conflicting or insufficiently established
                    I-->>U: Save and show a request for a distinguishing reference
                else Reuse a verified identity or create one after discovery
                    opt No suitable Execution Agent after active and archive search
                        I->>R: Create a saved Execution Agent record with a permanent ID
                    end
                    I->>R: Inspect this Execution Agent's identity, approvals,<br/>ongoing work status and current version
                    R-->>I: Current Execution Agent details and source references
                    I->>M: Journal the Interaction Agent's tool plan<br/>and stable operation key before submission
                    I->>Q: Submit instructions with the inspected<br/>Execution Agent ID and expected version
                    Q->>M: Persist this execution and current result-group membership
                    Q-->>I: Queued or rejected execution, with its reason
                end
            end
            I->>Q: Seal this result group when the Interaction Agent turn finishes
        end
    end
    rect rgb(219, 234, 254)
        Note over U,B: 2. Process Submitted Executions and Their Results
        Note over Q,E: Only submitted executions enter this section.<br/>Execution may start before its result group is sealed.<br/>Up to 100 concurrent executions, 100 queued executions,<br/>5-minute queue wait and 300-second execution timeout.<br/>At most one active execution per Execution Agent.
        loop While a submitted result group still needs processing
            loop Oldest runnable executions, up to 100 run concurrently
                Q->>E: Start a run for the assigned Execution Agent ID,<br/>busy or review-blocked Execution Agents do not block others
                E->>M: Load this Execution Agent's identity, ongoing work state<br/>and Agent Memory within 8,000 estimated tokens
                M-->>E: Earlier-work summary, recent complete request segments<br/>and references to this Execution Agent's original sources
                loop Up to 8 Execution Agent planning turns, until a final response or interruption
                    loop Each tool call selected in this planning turn
                        E->>M: Journal intent before each chosen tool call
                        alt Atomic Gmail operation or Trigger operation
                            E->>T: Execute the selected Gmail tool or Trigger tool
                            T-->>E: Tool result or uncertain external outcome
                        else Complex operation through the Search Email Task
                            E->>K: Run the Search Email Task
                            loop Up to 8 internal Search Email planning turns
                                opt Search Email requests Gmail queries
                                    K->>T: Run selected Gmail email-search queries
                                    T-->>K: Email search results
                                end
                            end
                            K->>K: Clean, deduplicate and select matching emails
                            K-->>E: Aggregated and cleaned email results
                        else Exact older evidence is needed
                            E->>M: Read this Execution Agent's source events,<br/>query excerpts or source pages
                            M-->>E: Bounded original evidence from its Agent Memory
                        end
                        E->>M: Preserve each full result, artifact or interruption evidence<br/>in this Execution Agent's Agent Memory
                    end
                end
                opt Execution reaches a final response
                    E->>R: Persist this Execution Agent's reported ongoing work state,<br/>pending draft approvals and active Triggers prevent completion
                end
                Note over E,T: An uncertain external write stops<br/>this execution immediately, before<br/>another tool call or model turn.
                E-->>Q: Execution result: response, success flag or review requirement
                Q->>M: Persist execution status and outcome,<br/>rejected and expired executions also count as terminal
            end
            Q->>I: Deliver this group's outcomes only after sealing<br/>and all its executions become terminal
            alt Another authorized step is necessary and follow-up is permitted
                I->>R: Repeat selection and current-version inspection<br/>from section 1 for every follow-up work item
                I->>M: Journal the follow-up tool plan and stable operation keys
                I->>Q: Submit follow-up executions in a new correlated result group
                I->>Q: Seal the new result group when this interaction turn finishes
                Note over I,Q: Reuse Execution Agent identities for continuing work.<br/>Reinspect if a version changes. Preserve user constraints.<br/>At most 5 follow-up stages and 20 total submissions<br/>per initiating request, rejected work cannot bypass limits.
            else No further authorized step, or fresh user direction is required
                I->>M: Save each reply or verbatim draft in Conversation Memory<br/>once using its stable event key
                I-->>U: Show outcomes, exact draft or required review,<br/>ask for approval before sending a prepared email draft
            end
            Note over I,Q: Repeat only when a follow-up result group was created.<br/>Terminal means succeeded, failed, expired, interrupted or rejected.<br/>An execution's success does not complete its ongoing work.<br/>Multiple tool calls can occur within one planning turn.
        end
    end
    rect rgb(255, 237, 213)
        Note over U,B: 3. Independent Background Activity
        Note over I,B: These services run independently of sections 1 and 2.<br/>An email notification is not new user authorization.
        opt Email Monitor finds an important email
            B->>I: Report the important-email summary
            I-->>U: Save and show a relevant notification or suggested action
        end
        opt Trigger Scheduler finds a due Trigger
            B->>Q: Submit instructions for the Execution Agent<br/>that owns this due Trigger, seal its result group
            Note over Q,B: Deduplicate by Trigger ID, scheduled time and reset generation.<br/>Project saved outcomes into the Trigger schedule.<br/>Process submitted executions through section 2.
        end
        B->>R: Maintenance refreshes embeddings for changed<br/>Execution Agent searchable fields
        B->>M: Maintenance summarizes completed Execution Agent request<br/>segments, separate summarization compacts Conversation Memory
        Note over R,M: Retain original source records after summarization.<br/>New Execution Agent search fields queue background indexing.<br/>Incomplete or failed indexing keeps discovery visibly degraded.
        B->>R: At startup and hourly, archive eligible Execution Agents<br/>completed and inactive for at least 30 days
        Note over R,B: Pending work, approvals, active Triggers, queued or running<br/>executions and unresolved interruptions prevent archival.<br/>Archived Execution Agents stay searchable, an accepted<br/>continuation reopens the same saved identity.
    end
    rect rgb(240, 253, 244)
        Note over U,B: 4. Backend Restart, Interrupted-Execution Review and History Reset
        opt Backend starts after a restart
            A->>Q: Classify previously running executions using<br/>their durable tool-effect journals before resuming work
            alt Journal proves safe read-only work with no unresolved write risk
                Q->>R: Leave the Execution Agent available,<br/>mark the lost execution failed and retryable
            else A write, unknown tool or missing evidence leaves uncertainty
                Q->>R: Mark the lost execution interrupted and its<br/>Execution Agent awaiting review, hold its queued follow-ups
            end
            Q->>Q: Expire overdue queued executions,<br/>resume only unexpired, eligible queued executions
            A->>I: Recover pending interaction turns from saved tool plans
            Note over I,Q: The Interaction Agent may submit one safe read-only retry<br/>per initiating request, subject to recorded retry eligibility.<br/>Never automatically repeat an uncertain external action.<br/>An uncertain write also stops a live execution immediately.
        end
        opt An interrupted execution requires explicit user resolution
            U->>I: Identify the interrupted execution and choose<br/>completed, abandon or retry
            I->>Q: Record the user's decision, retry creates a new execution,<br/>while completed or abandon releases eligible held work
            Note over I,Q: A reviewed retry runs before held follow-ups.<br/>A failed retry can still require review of the original action.
        end
        opt User chooses Clear History in the Chat UI
            U->>A: DELETE chat history through the backend API
            A->>B: Stop Email Monitor and Trigger Scheduler
            A->>I: Pause interaction admission and cancel pending interaction turns
            A->>B: Stop maintenance and both memory-summarization workers
            A->>Q: Stop submissions, drain executions for up to 30 seconds,<br/>then cancel remaining owned work
            A->>M: Advance reset generation, clear saved requests, executions,<br/>Execution Agent records, both memories and Triggers
            A->>I: Resume interaction admission under the new reset generation
            A->>Q: Restart the empty execution queue
            A->>B: Restart background services with the new reset generation
            Note over A,M: Clearing history is a reset, not restart recovery.<br/>Old callbacks cannot recreate cleared local state.<br/>External actions already in flight cannot be undone.
        end
    end
